What's going on?

00:28:38.477 --> 00:28:39.977
- Let me write you a note.

00:28:39.977 --> 00:28:42.357
Well, I don't know, Filipe,
if you could tell Dan

00:28:42.357 --> 00:28:44.344
to just, you know, any
parting thoughts for folks?

00:28:44.344 --> 00:28:45.667
- So you can hear me,

00:28:45.667 --> 00:28:47.607
I can't hear anything, unfortunately.

00:28:47.607 --> 00:28:49.747
But this is part of
this staying adaptable.

00:28:49.747 --> 00:28:50.697
So I'll tell you what I'm gonna do,

00:28:50.697 --> 00:28:52.317
I'm gonna put my phone number

00:28:52.317 --> 00:28:53.837
into this private chat that we have.

00:28:53.837 --> 00:28:55.317
If you're watching this, I
don't think you can see this.

00:28:55.317 --> 00:28:57.647
I hope not, otherwise everyone's
getting my phone number.

00:28:57.647 --> 00:29:00.977
But if you wanna call,
maybe we can do it this way.

00:29:00.977 --> 00:29:03.160
Or you can write out the
questions and I'll answer them.

00:29:04.437 --> 00:29:06.260
- All right, let's see the chat.

00:29:10.797 --> 00:29:12.747
- While we do this, can
I just say something?

00:29:12.747 --> 00:29:14.387
Now I'm just gonna monologue.

00:29:14.387 --> 00:29:17.547
I will say that we have on LinkedIn,

00:29:17.547 --> 00:29:20.097
we keep a running list
of jobs that are hiring.

00:29:20.097 --> 00:29:22.717
There are places that
are hiring right now.

00:29:22.717 --> 00:29:25.287
It might feel like that
no one is actually hiring.

00:29:25.287 --> 00:29:26.577
There are companies that are doing it.

00:29:26.577 --> 00:29:28.867
Target, Amazon, UPS, FedEx, McDonald's,

00:29:28.867 --> 00:29:30.787
Albertsons, Dollar General.

00:29:30.787 --> 00:29:32.947
There are big companies
that are trying to hire,

00:29:32.947 --> 00:29:35.630
that are continuing to
hire even in this pandemic.

00:29:38.675 --> 00:29:40.497
And I do want to talk about a survey

00:29:40.497 --> 00:29:42.837
that we did recently that
might be interesting,

00:29:42.837 --> 00:29:46.267
which is we looked at people
who had lost their jobs.

00:29:46.267 --> 00:29:48.827
And we talked to hiring
recruiters and hiring managers

00:29:48.827 --> 00:29:51.137
about what they were looking for.

00:29:51.137 --> 00:29:53.307
And a really interesting piece
of data came out of there,

00:29:53.307 --> 00:29:55.367
two interesting pieces
of data come out of this.

00:29:55.367 --> 00:29:57.377
One is that, people who
have lost their jobs

00:29:57.377 --> 00:30:02.377
are incredibly ashamed and embarrassed

00:30:02.507 --> 00:30:03.597
that they've lost their jobs.

00:30:03.597 --> 00:30:07.180
46% said they have lied
about being unemployed.

00:30:10.916 --> 00:30:12.737
And then when we talked
to hiring managers,

00:30:12.737 --> 00:30:14.797
they said they don't care

00:30:14.797 --> 00:30:16.027
whether someone is unemployed or not.

00:30:16.027 --> 00:30:18.647
It makes no difference to
them in terms of hiring

00:30:18.647 --> 00:30:22.277
and whether someone is currently employed.

00:30:22.277 --> 00:30:24.757
So there's this incredible mismatch

00:30:24.757 --> 00:30:28.297
in how people think about their work

00:30:31.119 --> 00:30:33.007
and what companies are looking for.

00:30:33.007 --> 00:30:35.517
That if you don't have a job,
it's okay not to have a job.

00:30:35.517 --> 00:30:36.987
What hiring managers just want to know

00:30:36.987 --> 00:30:38.627
is that you are continuing to stay busy,

00:30:38.627 --> 00:30:39.567
that you're trying new things,

00:30:39.567 --> 00:30:40.667
you're developing new skills,

00:30:40.667 --> 00:30:42.257
that you're continuing to post and share

00:30:42.257 --> 00:30:43.607
and explaining who you are.

00:30:44.777 --> 00:30:46.527
But it's not something to hide from.

00:30:46.527 --> 00:30:47.977
And I think that for a long time,

00:30:47.977 --> 00:30:50.537
we have been led to believe that

00:30:50.537 --> 00:30:53.117
you can only get a job if
you currently have a job,

00:30:53.117 --> 00:30:56.607
or that you need to put on a fake front

00:30:56.607 --> 00:30:58.457
and make it seem like
you're still working.

00:30:58.457 --> 00:30:59.607
It's just not true.

00:30:59.607 --> 00:31:01.820
The data says that this is not true.

00:31:03.707 --> 00:31:06.347
That having a job is not
the most important thing

00:31:06.347 --> 00:31:07.617
to getting your next job.

00:31:07.617 --> 00:31:10.497
It is staying active, showing
that you're still involved,

00:31:10.497 --> 00:31:12.717
that you are doing things
that are productive,

00:31:12.717 --> 00:31:15.647
and that you are someone that a company

00:31:15.647 --> 00:31:17.627
can get meaningful work out of,

00:31:17.627 --> 00:31:19.177
right as soon as they hire you.

00:31:21.167 --> 00:31:23.017
